[tool_result]Web search results for query: "tavorite LiNiSO4F LiCoSO4F electrochemical voltage lithium nickel sulfate fluoride cathode"  Links: [{"title":"ChemInform Abstract: Evaluation of Tavorite-Structured Cathode Materials for Lithium-Ion Batteries Using High-Throughput Computing. | Request PDF - In the current scenario, Li-ion batteries are no longer limited to portable electronic devices, but are rapidly gaining momentum...","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/231241024_ChemInform_Abstract_Evaluation_of_Tavorite-Structured_Cathode_Materials_for_Lithium-Ion_Batteries_Using_High-Throughput_Computing#5"},{"title":"Structure and electrochemical properties of novel mixed Li(Fe1−xMx)SO4F (M = Co, Ni, Mn) phases fabricated by low temperature ionothermal synthesis","url":"https://www.scilit.com/publications/278a82039d7993e7aed3ae613dbce261"},{"title":"Crystal and electronic structures of lithium fluorosulphate based materials for lithium-ion batteries","url":"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2010PhRvB..82l5101R/abstract"},{"title":"Structure and electrochemical properties of novel mixed Li(Fe 1-xMx)SO4F (M = Co, Ni, Mn) phases fabricated by low temperature ionothermal synthesis - Please use this identifier to cite or link to this item: https://hdl","url":"https://repository.hkust.edu.hk/ir/Record/1783.1-58503#1"},{"title":"Crystal and electronic structures of lithium fluorosulphate based materials for lithium-ion batteries","url":"http://kth.diva-portal.org/smash/record.jsf?pid=diva2%3A375812&dswid=6903"},{"title":"AVPO4F (A = Li, K): A 4 V Cathode Material for High-Power Rechargeable Batteries - CONTENT TYPES","url":"https://pubs-acs-org-443.webvpna.lzu.edu.cn/doi/full/10.1021/acs.chemmater.5b04065#1"},{"title":"First-Principles Calculations on the LiMSO4F/MSO4F (M = Fe, Co, and Ni) Systems - Loading [MathJax]/extensions/MathZoom","url":"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/jp111310g#1"}]  ## Summary  **Tavorite structure and theory**  The fluorosulfate family LiMSO₄F (M = Fe, Co, Ni) adopts the tavorite-type structure. Ab initio calculations found that LiCoSO₄F and LiNiSO₄F share a similar crystal structure with LiFeSO₄F, the latter having a calculated intercalation voltage of 3.69 V, in excellent agreement with experiment (Ramzan et al., *Phys. Rev. B*). LiFeSO₄F behaves as a 3D lithium-ion conductor (activation energy ~0.4 eV for long-range diffusion through zigzag paths in the open tavorite lattice), whereas the related NaFeSO₄F is only a 1D conductor.  **Calculated electrochemical voltages**  Systematic first-principles DFT calculations on LiMSO₄F/MSO₄F (M = Fe, Co, Ni) give theoretical intercalation voltages of:  - **3.54 V for LiFeSO₄F** - **4.73 V for LiCoSO₄F** - **5.16 V for LiNiSO₄F**  These are close to the corresponding LiMPO₄ phosphates (Xie et al., *J. Phys. Chem. C*). All LiMSO₄F compounds are in a high-spin antiferromagnetic ground state.  **Mechanism and stability concerns**  Upon Li⁺ extraction, a significant amount of electron charge transfer occurs on the oxygen anions, especially for LiCoSO₄F and LiNiSO₄F. For nickel specifically, charge rearrangement occurs between different d-orbitals with little net positive charge gain, while Co and Fe end up in a clear oxidized state; the enhanced oxygen participation in LiNiSO₄F partly explains the voltage increase from Fe to Ni. This oxygen charge transfer is flagged as an intrinsic drawback, potentially leading to significant oxygen loss and concerns about structural and thermal stability.  **Experimental findings**  Experimentally, ionothermally synthesized mixed phases Li(Fe₁₋ₓCoₓ)SO₄F, Li(Fe₁₋ₓNiₓ)SO₄F, and Li(Fe₁₋ₓMnₓ)SO₄F (plus end members LiCoSO₄F, LiNiSO₄F, LiMnSO₄F) showed only a **3.6 V Fe²⁺/³⁺ redox reaction, with no signature of Co²⁺/³⁺, Ni²⁺/³⁺, or Mn²⁺/³⁺ activity**, despite delivering near-theoretical capacity (Barpanda, Recham, Tarascon et al., *J. Mater. Chem.*, 2010). Thus, while theory predicts high voltages (~4.7–5.2 V) for the Co and Ni end members, the Co/Ni redox processes were not experimentally accessible in these mixed fluorosulfate systems.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.
